---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../site';
---

<Base title="Privacy" description="What redvars.com and its waitlist collect about visitors, and who else sees each visit.">
  <article class="container">
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p class="updated">Last updated 26 October 2026</p>

    <p>
      redvars.com is a static website with no accounts. It collects data about visitors in two ways: the waitlist form
      keeps what you enter in it, and Google Analytics records visits.
    </p>

    <h2>Waitlist</h2>
    <p>
      Joining the waitlist opens a form in Microsoft Forms, which Microsoft runs for our Microsoft 365 account. It asks
      for your email address and name and, if you choose, your company, your role and what you want to build. We use
      your answers only to invite you
      to Redvars and to write to you about it. To have them deleted, write to
      <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>. Microsoft's
      <a href="https://privacy.microsoft.com/privacystatement">privacy statement</a> covers how it handles the form.
    </p>

    <h2>Google Analytics</h2>
    <p>
      We use Google Analytics to count visits and see which pages people read. It sets cookies in your browser and
      sends Google your IP address, details of your browser and device, and the pages you visit. Google's
      <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">privacy policy</a> explains how it uses that data, and its
      <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout">opt-out browser add-on</a> stops it.
    </p>

    <h2>Services that deliver the site</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/pages/getting-started-with-github-pages/about-github-pages#data-collection">GitHub Pages</a>
        hosts the site and logs visitors' IP addresses for security.
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="https://www.jsdelivr.com/terms/privacy-policy-jsdelivr-net">jsDelivr</a> serves the Peacock components
        the pages are built with.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>Fonts are served from redvars.com itself.</p>

    <p>Questions about privacy go to <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.</p>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  article {
    padding-block: var(--spacing-600);
  }

  article > * {
    max-width: 44rem;
  }

  h1 {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: var(--typography-headline-large-font-size);
  }

  h2 {
    margin-top: var(--spacing-400);
    font-size: var(--typography-title-large-font-size);
  }

  .updated {
    margin-top: var(--spacing-100);
    color: var(--color-on-surface-variant);
    font-size: var(--typography-body-medium-font-size);
  }
</style>
